// Question bank for Biz, the daily business gauntlet. Imported ONLY by the
// server page (app/biz/page.js), which resolves the picked day's twenty-five
// questions and hands the client just that day, so the rest of the bank never
// reaches a browser.
//
//   id       'd<day>q<slot>' - authored day and play order (slot 1..25)
//   cat      one of five business lanes; each tier block covers all five,
//            always in the same order: Brands & Products, Markets & Money,
//            Founders & Bosses, Deals & Disasters, Business History
//   tier     1 (gimme) .. 5 (expert); a day ramps 5 questions per tier
//   choices  exactly four, one defensibly correct; the correct position came
//            from a per-day balanced no-3-run sequence at build time, so do NOT
//            hand-reorder choices here
//
// EVERY FACT IS FROZEN, and that is the rule this bank lives or dies by.
// Business questions rot faster than almost any other kind, because the answer
// keeps moving: a chief executive resigns, a brand changes hands, a share price
// halves, a "largest" becomes a second largest. So this bank asks only about
// settled things. Banned at authoring: who currently runs or owns anything,
// current prices, revenues, market caps, rankings or store counts, any present
// tense superlative, any pending deal, and any case still under appeal. A
// superlative that is genuinely worth asking gets pinned in the stem instead
// ("the best selling model of the 1990s", "what was then the second largest").
// Authored 2026-08-27 with nothing later than the 2024 calendar year.
//
// Extending the bank: author new days in the same shape (5 lanes x 5 tiers,
// gimme to expert), then run scripts/verify-biz.mjs. Never reuse an id or a
// question, and never let one day carry the same answer twice.
